@startuml TestingLayer2Contract
' SPEC source: cmd/proveo/main_test.go, cmd/proveo/golden_test.go, internal/contract/**
' Layer 2 — Go contract tests on real builders (replacing bash grep). No Docker.
' 2026-10-16: the runner package's DockerRunArgs golden, internal/egress BuildPlan
' goldens and writeBrokerEnv/sentinel cases are DELETED with the docker+egress
' backend; the sbx builders (sandbox.Spec, TestSandboxPlanGolden) carry the lane.
!includeurl https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/refs/heads/main/proveo.iuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

' purpose: the Layer-2 contract lane — Go builders executed and diffed against
'          goldens, replacing grep-for-substring contracts
' covers: internal/contract/**
' covers: cmd/proveo/*_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/*_test.go
' covers: internal/imagetest/**
'
'   the image suites ................ _spec/tests/testing-strategy.puml
'   maintainer tooling as mise tasks  _spec/cmd/proveo/usage.puml
'
' ── WHY HOST CODE IS GO (the operator's choice, 2026-09-22) ───────────────
' Host build, def tests, lib/ and scripts/ ran on macOS /bin/bash 3.2, and
' end users met it too: provision.go ran `bash build.sh` for a missing image.
' NOT CHOSEN: fish, which has no errexit and is non-POSIX at every Kit, sbx,
' Dockerfile and installer boundary; a mise-pinned bash 5, which never reaches
' an end user's stock 3.2. In-image bash STAYS: it only meets Debian bash 5,
' and sbx hooks, `sbx exec … bash -c` and Dockerfile RUN speak it, so moving
' it would add a boundary instead of removing one.
'
' ── HOST SHELL ALLOWLIST (internal/contract/host_bash_test.go) ─────────────
' MEASURED, host_bash_test.go:15-23:
' TestNoHostShellOutsideTheAllowlist walks `git ls-files` and refuses any
' shell-shebang file the operator's Mac could execute, except
'   apps/cli/public/cli/install.sh, uninstall.sh  bootstrap/remove proveo
'                                                 before it exists; guarded by
'                                                 installer_bash_test.go
' A stale entry fails too. The tracked post-commit shim left the list on
' 2026-11-12: the hook is mise's generated, untracked one
' (_spec/_devops/git-hooks.puml).
' TestMiseTasksRunNoShellScripts (2026-11-12) holds every mise.toml run string
' and skip_if to plain argv. mise 2026.10.17 runs each under `sh -o errexit
' -c` (MEASURED), so the rule bans the shell logic, not the hop. It is an
' allowlist: once Tera blocks and '…' argv words are stripped, a run string
' holds letters, digits, space and -_./=:,@+%^, with $ only at a word's end.
' Every {{ … }} ends in `| quote`, so a Tera value lands as one argv word;
' a boolean flag renders through {% if %} as a bare word. NOT CHOSEN: `|
' as_str | quote` on booleans (quote refuses a bool); quoting only free-form
' values (the scan cannot tell them apart).
' No non-ASCII, no leading VAR=, and the first word is no bash keyword or
' builtin (compgen -k -b), no shell and no env. TestShellLogicScanFlagsHandRolledShell
' pins the scan on both sides.
' The scan reads [tasks.<name>] tables alone, so it refuses the forms it
' cannot read: a [tasks] shorthand, a top-level tasks. key, a task sub-table
' or array of tables, and a task key outside its list, such as run_windows,
' file or shell (TestShellScanReadsEveryTaskShape).
' AN ALLOWLIST, NOT A DENYLIST (2026-11-12): extending a denylist lets the
' next construct slip through. The contract tests read mise.toml with a
' small hand-written reader. NOT CHOSEN: a TOML module in go.mod; shelling
' out to mise from unit tests.
' NO TASK PROBES WITH exec(). Tera's exec() renders with the caller's PATH,
' not the task's tools (MEASURED, mise 2026.10.17). So the race fallback is
' a --no-race flag, the untagged-HEAD check is a Go test
' (_spec/_devops/release-gate.puml), and GOBIN is a task env value.
' Trees whose shell runs in an image (bash 5) or is an agent's fixture are
' out of scope: defs/, packages/lib/, e2e/testdata/, e2e/samples/.
' Host code is Go; macOS /bin/bash 3.2 is on no host path.

title Layer 2 · Contract — Go builders + goldens (no Docker)

actor "go test ./cmd/... ./internal/...\n(mise run test)" as Runner <<actor>>

package "Contract suites (Go)" as Suites {
  component "cmd/proveo\nproviderLookup · sbx plan goldens\nposture golden" as CLI <<app>>
  component "internal/backend/sandbox\nsandbox.Spec — Kit, argv, secrets" as RunnerPkg <<app>>
  component "internal/provider\nregistry pins · Detect order" as Provider <<app>>
  component "internal/run\nrequireSandbox · egress row · Kit allow" as EgressPlan <<app>>
  component "internal/workspace\nmount plan · ProjectEnvFile" as Workspace <<app>>
  component "shim / Dockerfile\nstructural asserts (Go)" as Struct <<app>>
}

package "Image suites (opt-in, -tags=image)" as Bash {
  component "internal/imagetest\nTestImage<Def> · live-LLM checks skip without keys" as Residual <<app>>
}

package "Assertion targets" as Targets {
  component "defs/*/harness.manifest · Dockerfiles\nmise.toml · tracked shell files" as Defs <<app>>
  component "internal/* (executed, not grepped)" as GoSrc <<app>>
}

Runner --> Suites
Suites --> GoSrc : call / golden
Struct ..> Defs : parse / contain checks
Bash ..> Runner : not on default go test path

note bottom of Suites
**Go-first:** contracts execute builders (sandbox.Spec, Detect, the posture
and plan goldens) instead of grep-for-substring on source. That catches
regressions bash needles missed (e.g. host .env keys not reaching the broker,
when the broker was proveo's). Deterministic; no Docker.
end note

note right of Bash
Image and live-LLM checks are Go since 2026-09-22.
They need a built image, so default go test never
compiles them; the shell contract wrapper is
deleted.
end note
@enduml
